{%- doc -%}
  Store-wide sale rule, in one place. Returns the DISPLAY sale price in cents for one amount,
  or prints nothing when the sale does not apply.

  What it reads (Settings > Custom data > Shop metafields):
  - custom.sale_percent  whole number, 0 to 90. Empty or 0 = no sale.
  - custom.sale_ends     optional date and time. Once now is at or past it, no sale.

  The real discount is NOT created here. It comes from the automatic discount in
  Shopify Discounts, which is what the cart and checkout charge. This snippet only changes the
  prices SHOWN on product pages, cards, search and so on, so keep the two percentages the same.
  Rounding is to the nearest cent, like the discount in the cart.

  It does not apply to gift cards.

  Times are compared as epoch seconds so the shop timezone cannot skew the cut-off.

  @param {number} amount - Price in cents (a variant price, price_min, price_max)
  @param {product} product - The product the price belongs to (used to skip gift cards)

  @example
  {% capture sale_cents %}{% render 'storewide-sale', amount: variant.price, product: product %}{% endcapture %}
  {% assign sale_cents = sale_cents | plus: 0 %}
  {% if sale_cents > 0 %} ...show sale_cents... {% endif %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign sale_percent = shop.metafields.custom.sale_percent.value | plus: 0
  assign sale_is_on = false

  if sale_percent > 0 and product != blank and product.gift_card? != true and amount > 0
    assign sale_is_on = true
    assign sale_ends_at = shop.metafields.custom.sale_ends.value
    if sale_ends_at != blank
      assign sale_now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
      assign sale_ends_s = sale_ends_at | date: '%s' | plus: 0
      if sale_now_s >= sale_ends_s
        assign sale_is_on = false
      endif
    endif
  endif

  if sale_is_on
    assign sale_discount = amount | times: sale_percent | divided_by: 100.0 | round
    echo amount | minus: sale_discount
  endif
-%}
